; Tutorial_5_Mark_Filter_and_Sort.inix -- choosing records, narrowing the list, ordering it.

[about]
Title=5 - Mark, Filter and Sort
Intro=Records marked one at a time and in runs, the list narrowed by a filter, and put in order by a column.
Setup=JobTrail is open in DbDo.
Homework=Filter your own table to one value, then sort what is left.

[step]

Say=One want: only the jobs still waiting, the newest first.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Control plus D, D for DbDo, opens it or brings it forward.
Key=Alt+Control+D
Hear=DbDo
Hear=DbDo ready

[step]

Say=Control plus M, M for Mark, marks the record I am on, for a later command to act on.
Key=Control+M
Hear=Marked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Shift plus M asks about marks, changing nothing.
Key=Shift+M
Hear=(how many records are marked)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus Shift plus M reverses it: Shift reverses.
Key=Control+Shift+M
Hear=Unmarked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus F, F for Filter, shows only the records that match. It begins with a choice.
Key=Control+F
Hear=Filter Records dialog
Hear=Filter by: list box, Any field contains text, 1 of 2
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Any field is the first choice, so Enter alone takes it. It asks for the text to find, wherever it is.
Key=Enter
Hear=Any Field Contains dialog
Hear=Text to find in any field: edit
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I type Seattle and press Enter. Every job with Seattle in any field stays: the city, the address, the notes.
Key=Enter
Hear=3 records have Seattle.
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus F again. With a filter in force, the list offers more, each choice with its own first letter. N for Narrow keeps Seattle and adds a field.
Key=N
Hear=Narrow with the field form, 4 of 4
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Enter opens the form, a box for each field. I type waiting in the status box and press Enter.
Key=Enter
Hear=Filter applied. 2 records match.
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Shift plus F says the filter, both parts, in the words each was asked in.
Key=Shift+F
Hear=any field contains Seattle; and where: status = 'waiting'
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus O, O for Order, sorts by a column; I choose the date added.
Key=Alt+O
Hear=Order Records dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Enter sorts. Alt plus Shift plus O reverses the order, newest first.
Key=Alt+Shift+O
Hear=(the newest waiting job)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A planned misstep: the filter stays until it is cleared, so a later search finds only waiting jobs. Control plus Shift plus F clears it.
Key=Control+Shift+F
Hear=No filter
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Marking one record at a time is slow for many. F8 drops an anchor at the record I am on.
Key=F8
Hear=Mark anchor
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Down Arrow four records, then Shift plus F8 marks everything from the anchor to here.
Key=Shift+F8
Hear=5 records marked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus A marks every record, Control plus Shift plus A unmarks them all, and Alt plus Shift plus I swaps marked and unmarked.
Key=Control+Shift+A
Hear=All unmarked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Marks are for acting on: Delete, Copy and Export all work on the marked records when there are any. Shift plus Space reads every marked record in full, to check before acting.
Key=Shift+Space
Hear=No records are marked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=With a filter and an order in force, Shift plus 8 says both at once, so you always know what you are looking at.
Key=Shift+8
Hear=Sort: added, descending; Filter: any field contains Seattle; and status = 'waiting'
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Shift plus O says just the order, and Shift plus F just the filter.
Key=Shift+O
Hear=added, descending
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus Space toggles the mark on the record I am on, as it toggles a selection in any Windows list.
Key=Control+Space
Hear=Marked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=With a filter in force, Shift plus Y says how many records it leaves.
Key=Shift+Y
Hear=4 records
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus Shift plus L reads one column for the marked records only: here, the employers of the jobs I marked.
Key=Alt+Shift+L
Hear=Amazon, Costco
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A filter and marks work together: filter to narrow, mark to choose, then act on the marked.
Key=

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I name the command; the reader gives the key.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Mark, then unmark.
Key=
Hear=Control plus M
Hear=Control plus Shift plus M

[step]

Say=Filter, then clear it.
Key=
Hear=Control plus F
Hear=Control plus Shift plus F

[step]

Say=Order by a column.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus O
